## 🎯 Quick Checklist Before Launch

- [ ] All core flows (search, filter, cart, checkout) tested end‑to‑end.  
- [ ] Accessibility score ≥ 90% (Lighthouse).  
- [ ] Bundle size < 200 KB (after minification).  
- [ ] SEO meta tags, structured data (JSON‑LD).  
- [ ] Analytics & error monitoring set up.  
- [ ] Deployment pipeline automated.  

---

### Final Thought

Building a robust e‑commerce frontend is less about picking the “best” library and more about establishing a disciplined workflow: design first, code modularly, test relentlessly, and deploy continuously. With the stack and patterns above, you’ll have a maintainable, scalable foundation that can grow with your business—whether you’re adding new product categories, launching a mobile app, or integrating AI‑powered recommendations.

Happy coding! 🚀
